<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>\xi = \{x : x \text{ is a natural number}, x \le {10}\}</m>, <m>A = {\{1, 2, 3, 4, 6\}}</m> and <m>B = {\{4, 5, 6, 7\}}</m>.</p><p>List the elements of each set.</p><p>(a) <m>A'</m> <fillin characters="25" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) <m>A - B</m> <fillin characters="25" name="ans2"/>  </p><p>(c) <m>(A \cup B)'</m> <fillin characters="25" name="ans3"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p><m>\xi = \{1, 2, \ldots, {10}\}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>A'</m> is everything in <m>\xi</m> that is not in <m>A</m>: <m>A' = {\{5, 7, 8, 9, 10\}}</m>.</p><p>(b) Start with <m>A</m> and remove anything that is also in <m>B</m>, here <m>{\{4, 6\}}</m>: <m>A - B = {\{1, 2, 3\}}</m>.</p><p>(c) Brackets first: <m>A \cup B = {\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\}}</m>. Its complement is <m>(A \cup B)' = {\{8, 9, 10\}}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{5 , 7 , 8 , 9 , 10 \right \}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{1 , 2 , 3 \right \}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left \{8 , 9 , 10 \right \}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>